WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.740
Meet the Copper Crown.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:08.600
A stainless steel kettle sits inside an ornamental jacket,
above a protected electric heater.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.600
The crown begins with a band and a steel cone.
Steam will condense on its underside.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.600
A second cone sits a few millimeters above it,
under an open basin of cooling water.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.600
A riser carries leftover steam onward. A separate
open vent keeps the kettle at room pressure.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The leftover steam enters a descending coil in a second vessel.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Its cooling water never touches the product.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.800
Two free-draining lines end above an open glass carafe.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.600
Heat turns water into vapor.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.800
Under the first cone it condenses: the first harvest.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.800
The heat it gives up evaporates a film of feed water.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.800
That vapor crosses the gap and condenses
under the cap: the second harvest.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.500
One heat, two harvests.
